flow += [h('12. Scientific interpretation, reproducibility and references'),sh('What is established'),P('The original paceval MCP server successfully registered and reused versioned expressions for all the listed semiconductor-domain mathematical functions and evaluated them over the supplied synthetic datasets. Persistently handled math graphs produced independently checked values, distinct model decisions and representative TINC bounds. The C++ source defines original SDK and CSV integration and passes syntax-only compilation.'),sh('What remains outside the evidence'),P('This study does not contain real Liberty timing arcs, measured silicon, SPICE or path-aware waveform simulation, cell rise/fall asymmetry, setup/hold constraints, extracted RC parasitics, voltage droop, IR heating, multi-mode STA, LVF delay distributions or foundry signoff. The four-stage path is a mathematical demonstration only. The compatible Linux shared library was absent, so there are no CTest run results and no local SDK conversion execution. Future work may use openly licensed Liberty reference tables with careful model-to-table and EDA comparisons.'),sh('Reproduction commands'),P('From the project root, run <font name="DVS-Bold">python3 validation/validate_records.py</font> for the independent reference, <font name="DVS-Bold">python3 scripts/make_figures.py</font> for all result diagrams and <font name="DVS-Bold">python3 src/check_readme_math.py</font> for structural GitHub markdown and local link checks. For full original SDK integration, provide an ABI-compatible shared library and run <font name="DVS-Bold">bash scripts/build_and_test.sh /absolute/path/libpaceval_linux_sharedLIB.so</font>. No binary paceval library is shipped.'),sh('Selected external references'),P('[1] OpenSTA architecture, <link href="https://openroad.readthedocs.io/en/latest/main/src/sta/README.html" color="#148a8c">OpenROAD STA documentation</link>.','small'),P('[2] OpenSTA, <link href="https://openroad.readthedocs.io/en/latest/main/src/sta/doc/Examples.html" color="#148a8c">Multi-corner scenes and statistical timing examples</link>.','small'),P('[3] OpenSTA, <link href="https://openroad.readthedocs.io/en/latest/main/src/sta/doc/ChangeLog.html" color="#148a8c">Release 3.0.1, 12 March 2026 (LVF statistical analysis)</link>.','small'),P('[4] Arizona State University, <link href="https://asap.asu.edu/" color="#148a8c">ASAP7 predictive process design kit</link>.','small'),P('[5] Vashishtha et al., <i>ASAP7: A 7-nm finFET predictive process design kit</i>, Microelectronics Journal 53 (2016). <link href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mejo.2016.04.006" color="#148a8c">DOI</link>.','small'),P('[6] paceval, <link href="https://paceval.com/api/" color="#148a8c">Original SDK API</link> and <link href="https://paceval.com/product-brief/" color="#148a8c">documented operators</link>. The remote service reported v4.26.','small'),P('Conclusion: the synthetic, versioned paceval mathematical workflow is functionally demonstrated and independently checked. An EDA deployment or chip-signoff claim requires an entirely separate validation program.','small')]
